    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is heavily leveraged against Merrill Kelly today, making **Kyle Tucker** (81.11) and **Andy Pages** (74.84) our premier anchors. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill boost against Kelly\u2019s high-xERA profile, providing the safest floor for run production, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10) represents our most efficient value play; he draws an excellent matchup against Tyler Mahle, where his dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and favorable order slot provide an elite ceiling for our 5x5 targets. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tough test in Nathan Eovaldi, his elite lineup position at #1 and the nature of his dynamic platoon keep his projection firmly in the \u201cStrong\u201d category (64.29).\n\nStrategic depth remains a priority today, particularly regarding our middle infield and speed targets. **Nasim Nunez** (66.19) is a vital start, as his high-skill matchup against Petty and switch-hitting flexibility bolster his efficiency score, making him essential for our stolen base pursuit. The tightest decision on the bench was **Luis Lara** (47.02); while he possesses decent upside against Matthews, he ultimately fell short of the starting rotation because his efficiency metrics didn't clear the threshold required to displace the high-scoring floor of **Jacob Wilson** (59.71) or the top-tier matchup potential of our outfield core.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding external variables throughout the afternoon. **Jorge Polanco** (50.23) is a marginal play who carries a specific \u26a0\ufe0f Rain Risk (40%) at his venue, which could dampen his production or lead to a partial game; should that game be washed out, we have limited flexibility given the status of **Jordan Westburg** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** on the shelf. Additionally, both **Liam Hicks** and **Andy Pages** are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" designations; while our models assume their typical spots, any late adjustments to their batting order could necessitate a recalibration of their projected output.",
